    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1SA 14:49",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan, Ishvi, and Malchishua; and the names of his two daughters were these: the name of the firstborn Merab, and the name of the younger Michal."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 18:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Michal, Saul’s daughter, loved David; and they told Saul, and the thing pleased him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 18:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "David arose and went, he and his men, and killed two hundred men of the Philistines. Then David brought their foreskins, and they gave them in full number to the king, that he might be the king’s son-in-law. Then Saul gave him Michal his daughter as wife."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 18:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul saw and knew that the LORD was with David; and Michal, Saul’s daughter, loved him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 19:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul sent messengers to David’s house to watch him and to kill him in the morning. Michal, David’s wife, told him, saying, “If you don’t save your life tonight, tomorrow you will be killed.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 19:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Michal let David down through the window. He went away, fled, and escaped."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 19:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Michal took the teraphim and laid it in the bed, and put a pillow of goats’ hair at its head and covered it with clothes."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 19:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul said to Michal, “Why have you deceived me like this and let my enemy go, so that he has escaped?” Michal answered Saul, “He said to me, ‘Let me go! Why should I kill you?’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 25:44",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Saul had given Michal his daughter, David’s wife, to Palti the son of Laish, who was of Gallim."
      }
    ],
